you were given and the system's needs: follow those.

## The one rule

`make check` must pass before every commit. It checks that `go.mod` is tidy and
the code is formatted (gofumpt, goimports), then runs `go vet`, golangci-lint with
`.golangci.yml` and `go test -race`. CI runs the same command, and nothing reaches
`main` without it passing and a review. Never commit red.

